teach a small robot duck to move

Microduck is a two-legged robot, about 800 g and 25 cm tall. This repo lets you teach it through trial and error in a
physics simulator, then run what it learns on the real robot. It can learn to walk, get up after a fall, kick a ball
and roller skate.

This is a simplified fork of Pollen Robotics' original training code. They built the robot and did the original
research:

    https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck_rl
    https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck

You'll need a graphics card that supports CUDA, plus uv and make.

    make sync    # install
    make help    # list every target

Work with a coding agent. Have it read CLAUDE.md for the tasks, workflow and rules learned the hard way, then ask it
your questions.
